@startuml
!include ../../../tools/diagrams/cka-theme.puml
left to right direction
title A controller is a loop: watch, compare, act — forever

rectangle "Desired state\n<size:11>spec in the API</size>\n<size:11>e.g. replicas: 3</size>" <<accent>> as desired
rectangle "Actual state\n<size:11>what exists now</size>\n<size:11>e.g. 2 Pods running</size>" <<plain>> as actual

rectangle "Controller loop" <<groupGood>> as loop {
  rectangle "1 Watch\n<size:11>events from the</size>\n<size:11>kube-apiserver</size>" as watch
  rectangle "2 Compare\n<size:11>desired vs actual</size>" as diff
  rectangle "3 Act\n<size:11>create / delete / update</size>\n<size:11>through the API</size>" <<good>> as act
  watch --> diff
  diff --> act
}

desired --> watch
actual --> watch
act --> actual : 1 Pod created → 3 running

caption <i>In the harbor: the office watches its records, notices a container fell overboard, and orders a replacement.</i>\n<i>The loop never finishes; it keeps the two states equal, which is what "self-healing" means.</i>
@enduml
